From fc76cfbf69e4acb08a345b4acfc7b76476ddad06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:42:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] feat(helm): helm_list shows every release state;
 helm_uninstall names the state left; all-namespaces fallback (C12, C23,
 K8S-21)

After a failed helm_uninstall the release stays in `uninstalling`, and
helm_list answered "No Helm releases found": the tool used the Helm 3
SDK's default filter (deployed and failed only) and had no way to ask
for other states (K8S-21). On the native session (job 8) the agent
could not see what it had left. helm_list with all_namespaces failed
outright for an identity that may list release Secrets only in its own
namespace.

- helm_list lists every state by default (Helm 4's CLI default), so a
  release in uninstalling, pending-install/upgrade/rollback or failed
  is visible with its status. A new `states` argument (all, deployed,
  failed, pending, uninstalling, uninstalled, superseded, unknown)
  narrows it; an unknown state is refused.
- helm_list with all_namespaces, when the cluster-wide list is
  forbidden, says so and lists the current (or given) namespace
  instead (C23).
- A failed helm_uninstall now also names the state the release was
  left in and what to do (C12); Helm's own error already lists the
  objects it could not delete.

The default of helm_list changes what is listed (more states). Tests
cover the state filter and the fallback under an identity limited to
one namespace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
